              "section": "Who Pinealon Is For and Who Should Avoid It",
              "subsection": "",
              "excerpt": "Pregnancy and breastfeeding : safety has not been established. Avoid.",
              "truncated": false
            },
            {
              "section": "Who Pinealon Is For and Who Should Avoid It",
              "subsection": "",
              "excerpt": "Active cancer or recent cancer history : Pinealon affects apoptosis and caspase-3 signaling. Because caspase-3 has been linked to both tumor suppression and, in some contexts, tumor support, this group should avoid Pinealon outside formal oncology research.",
              "truncated": false
            },
            {
              "section": "Pinealon Side Effects & Safety",
              "subsection": "Theoretical or under-studied",
              "excerpt": "Long-term effects of repeated cycles have not been mapped in published Western trials.",
              "truncated": false
            },
            {
              "section": "Pinealon Side Effects & Safety",
              "subsection": "Theoretical or under-studied",
              "excerpt": "Pinealon's effect on caspase-3 signaling means cancer-related risk has not been ruled out in or out — researchers in oncology contexts generally exclude it.",
              "truncated": false
            },
            {
              "section": "FAQ",
              "subsection": "Q9: Who should avoid Pinealon?",
              "excerpt": "Pregnant or breastfeeding people, anyone with active cancer or a recent cancer history, anyone with a seizure disorder, children and teenagers, and anyone on prescription central nervous system medications should avoid Pinealon outside formal medical supervision.",
              "truncated": false
            }
